name 'building-data-driven-systems-postassessment-q4_2025'

question 'What is a significant privacy risk when using AI to help generate example data for a new app?'

wrong 'The AI might generate data that is too difficult for a human to read.'
right 'If you provide the AI with real user data as examples, that sensitive information could become part of the AI\'s training set.'
wrong 'The AI will charge you a fee for every piece of data it creates.'
wrong 'Using AI data makes it impossible to use the `.map()` method later.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 2

Sharing real, sensitive data with public AI tools can lead to data leaks. Developers should use "mock" or "synthetic" data when prompting AI to maintain privacy.
MARKDOWN
